{"vid":"D9jZMLm72a8","source":"D9jZMLm72a8.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":8,"txt":"Hello, this is 6 Minute English from BBC Learning English. I'm Neil."},{"t":11.8,"txt":"And I'm Pippa."},{"t":13.1,"txt":"When it comes to household chores, jobs like cleaning, washing clothes"},{"t":17.2,"txt":"or looking after the kids, it's often women who do most of the work."},{"t":21.7,"txt":"Here, two female listeners of BBC World Service programme"},{"t":25,"txt":"People Fixing the World share their experiences."},{"t":27.9,"txt":"Do they sound familiar to you?"},{"t":30.1,"txt":"I do everything. I do all the house chores,"},{"t":32.2,"txt":"I do the food shopping, I do all the cooking, I clean the bathroom."},{"t":37.6,"txt":"Are the chores done equally between me and my husband?"},{"t":41.8,"txt":"No, they're not done equally."},{"t":43.8,"txt":"I do most of the chores."},{"t":46.2,"txt":"So, you're a family man, Neil."},{"t":48.4,"txt":"Do you do your fair share of household chores?"},{"t":51.7,"txt":"I think so."},{"t":53.1,"txt":"My wife works part time and I work full time,"},{"t":56.6,"txt":"so when I'm not working, I do things,"},{"t":60,"txt":"and when she's not working, she does things."},{"t":62.4,"txt":"Yeah, it's similar in my house, so me and my husband try to split things,"},{"t":68,"txt":"but it's difficult, isn't it?"},{"t":69.2,"txt":"It is."},{"t":70,"txt":"Of course, no one enjoys cleaning the toilet or taking out the bins,"},{"t":74.2,"txt":"but there is a serious side to the issue."},{"t":76.9,"txt":"Figures from UN Women, an organisation promoting gender equality,"},{"t":81.2,"txt":"suggest that every day women around the world spend three hours more"},{"t":85.3,"txt":"than men on unpaid care and domestic work."},{"t":87.9,"txt":"So, in this episode, we'll be hearing about two projects helping husbands"},{"t":92.4,"txt":"and wives share the housework more fairly."},{"t":95.1,"txt":"And as usual, you'll find a quiz and a worksheet to go with this episode"},{"t":99.2,"txt":"on our website, bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":102.5,"txt":"But now I have a question for you, Pippa."},{"t":105.2,"txt":"According to a survey conducted by Good Housekeeping magazine earlier this year,"},{"t":110,"txt":"what is the most hated household chore in Britain?"},{"t":114.5,"txt":"Is it: a) deep cleaning the oven, b) scrubbing the toilet,"},{"t":119.6,"txt":"or c) cleaning the windows?"},{"t":122.2,"txt":"Hmm. I'm going to say deep cleaning the oven because I really hate that job."},{"t":127.4,"txt":"I hardly ever do it."},{"t":129.5,"txt":"I don't like any of those,"},{"t":130.6,"txt":"but we'll find out the answer at the end of the programme."},{"t":134.6,"txt":"Now, the first project we're going to look at is on"},{"t":137.2,"txt":"the remote Indonesian island of Rote."},{"t":140.3,"txt":"Here, men traditionally work as rice farmers or fishermen,"},{"t":144.1,"txt":"while women look after the home, the children and older people."},{"t":148.2,"txt":"But with few washing machines and no running water,"},{"t":151.2,"txt":"these domestic chores take a long time."},{"t":154,"txt":"The NGO ARUNGI runs a project trying to change attitudes"},{"t":158.2,"txt":"about the role of the island's women."},{"t":160.2,"txt":"They work alongside community leaders like Mama Shilpa,"},{"t":163.5,"txt":"who spoke with BBC World Service reporter Ade Mardiyati."},{"t":167.4,"txt":"It is expected that the tasks done in the house,"},{"t":171.4,"txt":"like holding the child, feeding the child, washing dishes, cooking,"},{"t":176.1,"txt":"will all be done by the mother."},{"t":179,"txt":"Shilpa tells me these are all considered women's work."},{"t":182.4,"txt":"And you might be thinking, Well, the man is busy in the fields,"},{"t":186.9,"txt":"so it's just a fair division of labour."},{"t":189.5,"txt":"But Shilpa tells me women also help out in the fields."},{"t":194,"txt":"On Rote, cleaning, cooking and sweeping"},{"t":196.7,"txt":"are considered women's work – a negative term"},{"t":199.7,"txt":"for boring and repetitive tasks which are traditionally done by women."},{"t":203.8,"txt":"Many cultures have a division of labour – a way of organising work"},{"t":208.3,"txt":"where different tasks are done by different groups of people."},{"t":211,"txt":"But on Rote this means women work even harder, helping out"},{"t":215,"txt":"with the farming and fishing too."},{"t":217.3,"txt":"You might think this only happens in traditional societies,"},{"t":220.5,"txt":"but research suggests that women in wealthy countries also spend"},{"t":224.7,"txt":"much more time on unpaid care work than men."},{"t":228.3,"txt":"One such country is Croatia,"},{"t":230.5,"txt":"where the NGO Status M run their Superdads project."},{"t":234.8,"txt":"Project worker Anamarija Soča leads workshops encouraging dads"},{"t":239.4,"txt":"and sons to take some of the pressure off mums."},{"t":242.6,"txt":"Here, she explains the benefits of this to the BBC World Service."},{"t":246.7,"txt":"Mothers have, you know,"},{"t":248.6,"txt":"of course, more space for their careers, or hobbies,"},{"t":252.7,"txt":"or just simply to rest – I mean, just to take a breather."},{"t":256.2,"txt":"Women tend to especially appreciate men who do these kinds of chores."},{"t":262.6,"txt":"And when they start pulling their weight,"},{"t":265.3,"txt":"then they jokingly say that, yeah, women tend to nag less."},{"t":270.7,"txt":"Sometimes mums need to take a breather – an informal way"},{"t":274.1,"txt":"of saying stop and rest a while."},{"t":276.4,"txt":"Anamarija also thinks women appreciate it"},{"t":278.9,"txt":"when their husbands pull their weight."},{"t":281.1,"txt":"If you pull your weight, you work as hard as everyone else."},{"t":284.6,"txt":"Both these NGO projects agree about one thing – men doing more to help"},{"t":289.5,"txt":"around the house results in happier homes,"},{"t":292,"txt":"even if that means cleaning the toilet now and then."},{"t":294.7,"txt":"And speaking of cleaning the toilet,"},{"t":296.8,"txt":"what was the answer to your quiz question, Neil?"},{"t":299.5,"txt":"I asked you what chore is the most hated in Britain."},{"t":303.7,"txt":"I thought it was cleaning the oven."},{"t":306,"txt":"Well, I'm afraid that's not the right answer."},{"t":308.6,"txt":"People hate cleaning the windows even more than scrubbing the oven."},{"t":312.8,"txt":"Apparently, 23% of the people who did the survey said cleaning the windows."},{"t":318.7,"txt":"OK. Let's recap the vocabulary we've learned,"},{"t":320.9,"txt":"starting with 'chores' – household tasks like cleaning, washing"},{"t":324.9,"txt":"and ironing that have to be done regularly."},{"t":327.6,"txt":"If you do your fair share of work, you do a reasonable amount."},{"t":332,"txt":"'Women's work' is a negative term for"},{"t":334.3,"txt":"the boring and repetitive tasks which are stereotypically done by women."},{"t":339.1,"txt":"The 'division of labour' is a way of organising work"},{"t":342.2,"txt":"where different tasks are done by different groups of people."},{"t":345.2,"txt":"The idiom 'take a breather' means to stop what you're doing"},{"t":348.2,"txt":"for a short time and rest."},{"t":350,"txt":"And finally, if you pull your weight, you work as hard"},{"t":353.4,"txt":"as everyone else doing the same job."},{"t":355.8,"txt":"Once again, our six minutes are up, but remember,"},{"t":358.3,"txt":"you can find a free transcript including all the vocabulary on our website,"},{"t":362.5,"txt":"at bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":364.5,"txt":"Goodbye for now."},{"t":365.5,"txt":"Goodbye!"}],"words":[{"t":7.96,"w":"Hello,"},{"t":7.96,"w":"this"},{"t":7.96,"w":"is"},{"t":7.96,"w":"6"},{"t":7.96,"w":"Minute"},{"t":7.96,"w":"English"},{"t":7.96,"w":"from"},{"t":7.96,"w":"BBC"},{"t":7.96,"w":"Learning"},{"t":7.96,"w":"English."},{"t":7.96,"w":"I'm"},{"t":7.96,"w":"Neil."},{"t":11.76,"w":"And"},{"t":11.76,"w":"I'm"},{"t":11.76,"w":"Pippa."},{"t":13.08,"w":"When"}